On Jul 25, 2:19=A0pm, Jistan Idiot <jistanid...@gmail.com> wrote:
> My next question is...
> Will a blessed scroll of magic mapping show me the stairs even if it
> is covered by something?

     Blessed magic mapping is the same as uncursed, so the
answer is probably no.  More specifically, if you haven't seen
the "something", then yes.  But if you have seen (or detected)
it, then the remembered object takes precedence over whatever
terrain is underneath it and continues to appear on your map.

     If you're really desperate, you could read a scroll of
amnesia first.  But that has other bad side-effects besides
forgetting the map (and seen objects) of the current level.


